"Norway 3-2 Senegal | Match report and highlights (https://www.fifa.com/en/tournaments/mens/worldcup/canadamexicousa2026/articles/norway-senegal-match-report-highlights)\nciteturn3142search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: 4 days ago; Image: EAST RUTHERFORD, NEW JERSEY - JUNE 22: Erling Haaland #9 of Norway scores his team's second goal during the FIFA World Cup 2026 Group I match between Norway and Senegal at New York New Jersey Stadium on June 22, 2026 in East Rutherford, New Jersey.\n\n# Haaland helps fire Norway into knockouts\n\nPublished\n    23 Jun 2026\n\nNorway v Senegal | Group I | FIFA World Cup 2026™ | Highlights\n\nWatch highlights of the match between Norway and Senegal played at New York/New Jersey Stadium on Monday 22 June at 20:00 (local time).Watch highlights of the match between Norway and Senegal played at New York/New Jersey Stadium on Monday 22 June at 20:00 (local time).\n\nA brace from Erling Haaland secured Norway a spot in the Round of 32, as well as keeping the striker in the adidas Golden Boot race.\n\n## Norway 3-2 Senegal\n\nNorway goals: Holmgren Pedersen (43), Haaland (48, 58)\nSenegal goals: Sarr (53, 90+3)\n\nErling Haaland was once again among the goals as Norway ensured progression to the Round of 32 at the FIFA World Cup 2026™ with a 3-2 win over Senegal.\n\nThe prolific marksman made it four goals in two World Cup games and an astonishing 59 in 52 for his country, with Marcus Holmgren Pedersen also on the scoresheet for Norway.\n\nChances were at a premium in a tight first half at New York/New Jersey Stadium, but Norway started to click as the interval approached and took the lead in the 43rd minute when Holmgren Pedersen capitalised upon a Kalidou Koulibaly error and gleefully lashed home.\n\nImage: EAST RUTHERFORD, NEW JERSEY - JUNE 22: Erling Haaland #9 of Norway scores his team's second goal during the FIFA World Cup 2026 Group I match between Norway and Senegal at New York New Jersey Stadium on June 22, 2026 in East Rutherford, New Jersey. (Photo by Maddie Meyer - FIFA/FIFA via Getty Images)\n\nHaaland then got his customary goal three minutes after the restart, calmly slotting in after an inch-perfect pass from Martin Odegaard to ensure he has now scored in each of his last 12 competitive appearances for Norway.\n\nIsmaila Sarr pulled one back for Senegal in the 53rd minute, but Haaland re-established Norway's two-goal advantage five minutes later when he poked in from close range.\n\nSarr made Norway sweat when he struck again in stoppage time, but Stale Solbakken's side held on for the victory they needed to secure a knockout berth with one group-stage game remaining.\n\nHaaland, meanwhile, is firmly involved in a mouthwatering tussle for the adidas Golden Boot with Lionel Messi and Kyian Mbappe.\n\n### Key stat\n\nThis win means Norway’s four FIFA World Cup victories have come against teams from four different confederations: 1-0 against Mexico (Concacaf) in 1994, 2-1 against Brazil (CONMEBOL) in 1998, 4-1 against Iraq (AFC) in 2026 and now a triumph against CAF representative Senegal.\n\n* * *\n\n### Michelob Ultra Superior Player of the Match\n\nErling Haaland (Norway)\n\nHaaland: The support we got today was incredible\n\nThe Norwegian forward reacted to his side's 3-2 win over Senegal and praised the nation's lively travelling support.The Norwegian forward reacted to his side's 3-2 win over Senegal and praised the nation's lively travelling support.\n\n### What they said...\n\n\"It was tough. We're a little disappointed. But it's not over yet, there's still a third game to play. We're going to go there to win it, and we're going to work hard.\"\nIsmaila Sarr, Senegal forward\n\n\"It was special again. Another amazing night and I'm super proud. I'm enjoying it a lot. I've enjoyed playing for Norway ever since my debut and you can see that. The World Cup is nice!\"\nErling Haaland, Norway forward--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHyundai Goal of the Tournament | Haaland wins Round of 16 vote (https://www.fifa.com/en/articles/haaland-voted-best-goal-round-of-16-hyundai)\nciteturn3142search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; Image: EAST RUTHERFORD, NEW JERSEY - JULY 05: Erling Haaland #9 of Norway scores his team's second goal during the FIFA World Cup 2026 Round of 16 match between Brazil and Norway at New York New Jersey Stadium on July 05, 2026 in East Rutherford, New Jersey. ... There will be two subsequent votes, following the same process after the quarter-finals and semi-finals (combined), and then a final vote at the end of the tournament.\n\n# Haaland's hammer voted best goal from Round of 16\n\nPublished\n    10 Jul 2026\n\nPlay Video\n\nErling Haaland (Brazil v Norway)\n\nHyundai Goal of the Tournament shortlist\n\nNorway international's second strike in the 2-1 victory over Brazil has won the third phase of voting for the Hyundai Goal of the Tournament award.\n\nErling Haaland has announced himself on the global stage during FIFA World Cup 2026™ with seven goals so far at his first tournament, including two in the enthralling victory against five-time winners Brazil at New York New Jersey Stadium on 5 July.\n\nFootball fans around the world have now ensured that his second in that game has a place among the official contenders for the Hyundai Goal of the Tournament award by selecting it as the winner of the poll for the Round of 16’s finest strike.\n\nHaaland had already headed his side into the lead by rising above Gabriel Magalhaes in the 79th minute. Then, with the stadium clock having ticked up to 90, the powerful Manchester City forward received the ball on the corner of the Brazil box, taking one touch with his right, a second with his left to set himself and then a third thunderbolt which sent the ball arrowing across the helpless Alisson and into the bottom corner of the net.\n\nHaaland's goal received 34 per cent of the vote from FIFA.com users around the globe, putting him ahead of Lionel Messi (25 per cent) after the Argentina skipper's sensational equaliser against Egypt, with Morocco's Azzedine Ounahi in third (16 per cent) following his well-worked effort from a set-piece against Canada.\n\nStale Solbakken's side held on through added time, despite a last-gasp Neymar penalty, and now take on England in Miami on Saturday, 11 July, with a World Cup semi-final against either Argentina or Switzerland firmly in their sights.\n\nImage: EAST RUTHERFORD, NEW JERSEY - JULY 05: Erling Haaland #9 of Norway scores his team's second goal during the FIFA World Cup 2026 Round of 16 match between Brazil and Norway at New York New Jersey Stadium on July 05, 2026 in East Rutherford, New Jersey. (Photo by Al Bello/Getty Images)\n\n## Hyundai Goal of the Tournament\n\n* * *\n\nThis is the third step in the process towards deciding the Hyundai Goal of the Tournament. There will be two subsequent votes, following the same process after the quarter-finals and semi-finals (combined), and then a final vote at the end of the tournament. With each voting window, FIFA.com users have 48 hours to place their vote.\n\nThe winner of the vote for the favourite goal of the group stage was Uzbekistan captain Eldor Shomurodov for his effort against Congo DR, before Sidny Lopes Cabral’s wonder-goal for Cabo Verde against Argentina topped the polls in the Round of 32.\n\n* * *\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFrom packed stadiums to record digital reach: FIFA World Cup 2026™ numbers tell story of unprecedented scale as last eight confirmed (https://inside.fifa.com/organisation/media-releases/packed-stadiums-record-digital-reach-world-cup-2026-numbers-unprecedented-scale?trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block)\nciteturn3142search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: 6 days ago; A total of 280 goals were scored in the 96 matches of the FIFA World Cup 2026, averaging 2.92 goals per game. ... Enzo Fernández’s winning goal in the match between Argentina and Egypt was the 3,000^{th} goal in the history of the FIFA World Cup. ... The record breakers Lionel Messi (ARG) has scored eight goals, while Kylian Mbappé (FRA) and Erling Haaland (NOR) have each scored seven.\nGoals\n\nA total of 280 goals were scored in the 96 matches of the FIFA World Cup 2026, averaging 2.92 goals per game. Argentina are in the lead with 14 goals. There were 23 goals in the eight round-of-16 matches, averaging 2.88 per game.\n\nLionel Messi (ARG) tops the all-time scoring chart in FIFA World Cup history with 21 goals, followed by Kylian Mbappé (FRA) with 19. Enzo Fernández’s winning goal in the match between Argentina and Egypt was the 3,000^{th} goal in the history of the FIFA World Cup. Disciplinary\n\nSo far, a total of 259 yellow cards have been shown (2.70 on average), and 14 expulsions (0.15 on average) have been recorded.\n\nThe record breakers Lionel Messi (ARG) has scored eight goals, while Kylian Mbappé (FRA) and Erling Haaland (NOR) have each scored seven. This is the first time in the history of the FIFA World Cup that three players have each scored seven or more goals in a single edition.\n\nMeanwhile, Mbappé has extended his record for goals scored in FIFA World Cup knockout matches to 11, surpassing all other players.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCopa do Mundo: Brasil 0 x 2 Noruega - Resumo do jogo (https://www.fifa.com/pt/tournaments/mens/worldcup/canadamexicousa2026/articles/brasil-noruega-resumo-melhores-momentos-oitavas?searchOverlay=1)\nciteturn3142search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; Image: EAST RUTHERFORD, NEW JERSEY - JULY 05: Erling Haaland #9 of Norway scores his team's first goal during the FIFA World Cup 2026 Round of 16 match between Brazil and Norway at New York New Jersey Stadium on July 05, 2026 in East Rutherford, New Jersey.\n\n# Noruega vence e elimina Brasil nas oitavas com dois gols de Haaland\n\nPublicado\n    5 jul 2026\n\nBrasil x Noruega | Oitavas de final | Copa do Mundo da FIFA 2026™ | Melhores momentos Brasil x Noruega | Oitavas de final | Copa do Mundo da FIFA 2026™ | Melhores momentos\n\nVeja os melhores momentos do jogo entre Brasil e Noruega, disputado no Estádio de Nova York-Nova Jersey, no domingo, 5 de julho, às 16h00 (horário local).Veja os melhores momentos do jogo entre Brasil e Noruega, disputado no Estádio de Nova York-Nova Jersey, no domingo, 5 de julho, às 16h00 (horário local).\n\nO grande artilheiro da Noruega fez a diferença por sua equipe de novo nas oitavas da Copa do Mundo da FIFA 2026™, com dois gols que eliminaram a Seleção Brasileira.\n\n## Brasil 1 x 2 Noruega\n\nGol do Brasil: Neymar (45'+10 do 2ºT) Gols da Noruega: Erling Haaland (34' e 45' do 2ºT)\n\n* * *\n\nA Noruega venceu o Brasil por 2 a 1 nas oitavas de final, com dois gols de Erling Haaland no segundo tempo, e avançou para as quartas da Copa do Mundo da FIFA 2026™ – consequentemente, causando a eliminação da Seleção Brasileira. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nErling Haaland and Norway shine as Cristiano Ronaldo meeting looms (https://www.fifa.com/en/articles/haaland-norway-denmark-nations-league)\nciteturn3142search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 weeks ago; Crawled: today; The FIFA World Cup 2026™ may be over, but Erling Haaland's red-hot form clearly isn't. ... Norway, who stunned Brazil on their way to a first-ever World Cup quarter-final over the summer, stayed remarkably composed under pressure after conceding the equaliser. ... Once again, Haaland was at the centre of it all, with his winning goal marking his 64th in 56 caps for Norway.\n\n# Haaland and Norway keep good times rolling\n\nPublished\n    25 Sep 2026\n\nIn their first competitive match since a superb World Cup campaign, Norway celebrated a win over Denmark and were once again able to count on their superstar striker.\n\nThe FIFA World Cup 2026™ may be over, but Erling Haaland's red-hot form clearly isn't. The superstar striker scored twice as Norway beat Denmark 3-2 at Ullevaal Stadion on Thursday evening, giving the nation their first win over their neighbours in 26 years.\n\nEarly goals from Oscar Bobb and Haaland had Norway cruising, before Denmark hit back through Mikkel Damsgaard and Rasmus Hojlund to level the score midway through the second half. But Norway recovered quickly: after a triple substitution and a well-rehearsed corner routine, it was Haaland who struck the winner in the 74th minute.\n\n\"We showed our top level a few times in that first half,\" forward Antonio Nusa told TV2. \"My assist [for Haaland's first goal] was pretty much a gift, I'd say. I do my job and try to set him up as well as I can. And I know that when he shoots, it's most likely a goal.\"\n\nFor Stale Solbakken's side, it was their eighth straight competitive win at Ullevaal and proof that the team's strong development over the last year shows no sign of slowing.\n\nNorway, who stunned Brazil on their way to a first-ever World Cup quarter-final over the summer, stayed remarkably composed under pressure after conceding the equaliser. It was another reminder that, alongside Haaland, Norway have another player with serious leadership qualities in Martin Odegaard: the captain rallied the crowd, and the stadium responded with one of the loudest roars it has produced in a long time. Moments later, Norway turned the game back in their favour.\n\nFor coach Solbakken, it was evidence that his side have carried the confidence gained over the summer into their everyday form. Once again, Haaland was at the centre of it all, with his winning goal marking his 64th in 56 caps for Norway. He has been his country's all-time top scorer since October 2024, and if he keeps up this rate, he will push the bar to almost unimaginable heights.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nالبرازيل 1-2 النرويج | تقرير المباراة وأبرز اللقطات | كأس العالم 2026 (https://www.fifa.com/ar/tournaments/mens/worldcup/canadamexicousa2026/articles/brazil-norway-match-report-highlights-ar?searchOverlay=1)\nciteturn3142search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: last month; Image: EAST RUTHERFORD, NEW JERSEY - JULY 05: Erling Haaland #9 of Norway leads teammates in the Viking Row to celebrate the 2-1 victory during the FIFA World Cup 2026 Round of 16 match between Brazil and Norway at New York New Jersey Stadium on July 05, 2026 in East Rutherford, New Jersey.\n\n# النرويج تُقصي البرازيل بثنائية هالاند وتتأهل إلى ربع النهائي\n\nتم النشر\n    5 يوليو 2026\n\nتأهل منتخب النرويج إلى دور الثمانية في كأس العالم للمرة الأولى في تاريخه، بعد فوزه على البرازيل بفضل ثنائية إرلينج هالاند وأداء أورجان نيلاند الرائع.\n\n## البرازيل 1-2 النرويج\n\nهدف البرازيل: نيمار (90+9) أهداف النرويج: إرلينغ هالاند (79، 90)\n\nحققت النرويج إنجازًا تاريخيًا بتأهلها إلى ربع نهائي كأس العالم FIFA للمرة الأولى في تاريخها، بعدما تغلبت على البرازيل بنتيجة 2-0، في المباراة التي جمعتهما ضمن منافسات دور الـ16.\n\nوصمد المنتخب النرويجي أمام الضغط البرازيلي طوال معظم فترات اللقاء، مستفيدًا من تألق حارس مرماه أورجان نيلاند، الذي لعب دورًا حاسمًا في الحفاظ على نظافة شباكه.\n\nوجاءت لحظة الحسم في الدقيقة 79، عندما انطلق البديل أندرياس شيلديروب من الجهة اليسرى بعد هجمة جماعية مميزة، قبل أن يرسل عرضية متقنة ارتقى لها إرلينغ هالاند، ليحولها برأسه إلى الشباك معلنًا تقدم النرويج.\n\nوفي الوقت بدل الضائع، أضاف هالاند الهدف الثاني، بعدما سدد كرة مرت بين ساقي المدافع دانيلو وعجز الحارس أليسون عن التصدي لها، رافعًا رصيده إلى 7 أهداف في البطولة.\n\nوفي الدقيقة 90+7، حصلت البرازيل على ركلة جزاء ترجمها نيمار دا سيلفا إلى هدف تقليص الفارق، ولكن الوقت لم يسعف السيليساو للعودة في النتيجة، لتنتهي المواجهة بفوز النرويج بهدفين مقابل هدف.\n\nوبهذه النتيجة، ودعت البرازيل البطولة من دور الـ16، في أول خروج لها من هذا الدور منذ 1990، بينما سيواجه منتخب النرويج، بقيادة المدرب ستوله سولباكن، في الدور المقبل الفائز من مواجهة المكسيك وإنجلترا، في مباراة تُقام بمدينة ميامي يوم 11 يوليو/تمّوز.\n\n#### إحصائيات مميزة\n\n  * رفع إرلينغ هالاند رصيده إلى سبعة أهداف في أربع مباريات خاضها في كأس العالم 2026.\n\n  * سجل هالاند 62 هدفًا في 54 مباراة بقميص منتخب النرويج.\n\n  * هز هالاند الشباك في آخر 14 مباراة رسمية متتالية خاضها مع منتخب النرويج، مسجلًا خلالها 27 هدفًا.\n\n* * *\n\n#### جائزة Michelob Ultra لأفضل لاعب في المباراة\n\nإرلينغ هالاند (النرويج)\n\n* * *\n\n#### تصريحات ما بعد المباراة..\n\n\"أعتقد أن كل من يحمل الجنسية النرويجية يمكنه الاستمتاع بهذه الليلة. كانت مباراة مثيرة للغاية، وكان بإمكان أي من المنتخبين حسمها. لكننا قدمنا مباراة قوية من الناحية التكتيكية. ارتكبنا بعض الأخطاء في فقدان الكرة وكان من الممكن أن تكلفنا الكثير، لكن في النهاية سارت الأمور لصالحنا، ويجب أن نشعر بفخر كبير بما حققناه\". --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCosta do Marfim 1 x 2 Noruega | Resumo e melhores momentos (https://www.fifa.com/pt/tournaments/mens/worldcup/canadamexicousa2026/articles/costa-do-marfim-noruega-resumo-melhores-momentos-segunda-fase)\nciteturn3142search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; Image: ARLINGTON, TEXAS - JUNE 30: Erling Haaland #9 of Norway celebrates with teammates after scoring the team's second goal during the FIFA World Cup 2026 Round Of 32 match between Cote d'Ivoire and Norway at Dallas Stadium on June 30, 2026 in Arlington, Texas.\n\n# Haaland decide, Noruega elimina Costa do Marfim e será adversária do Brasil nas oitavas\n\nPublicado\n    30 jun 2026\n\n\nAudio\n\nCosta do Marfim x Noruega | 16-avos de final | Copa do Mundo da FIFA 2026™ | Melhores momentos Costa do Marfim x Noruega | 16-avos de final | Copa do Mundo da FIFA 2026™ | Melhores momentos\n\nVeja os melhores momentos do jogo entre Costa do Marfim e Noruega, disputado no Estádio de Dallas, na terça-feira, 30 de junho, às 12h00 (horário local).Veja os melhores momentos do jogo entre Costa do Marfim e Noruega, disputado no Estádio de Dallas, na terça-feira, 30 de junho, às 12h00 (horário local).\n\nCentroavante marca pela quinta vez na Copa e coloca nórdicos no caminho canarinho; partida será neste domingo\n\n## Costa do Marfim 1 x 2 Noruega | 16-avos de final\n\nGol da Costa do Marfim: Amad Diallo (29' do 2º tempo) Gols da Noruega: Antonio Nusa (39' do 1º tempo) e Erling Haaland (41' do 2º tempo)\n\nA Noruega será a próxima adversária do Brasil em sua tentativa de conquistar o hexacampeonato mundial.\n\nA equipe do craque Erling Haaland conquistou a classificação para enfrentar a Seleção no próximo domingo, em Nova York/Nova Jersey, pelas oitavas de final da Copa do Mundo da FIFA 2026 ao vencer um confronto eliminatório cheio de reviravoltas com a Costa do Marfim.\n\nApós abrir o placar no primeiro tempo, os escandinavos cederam o empate na segunda etapa e foram buscar a vitória, já depois dos 40 minutos da etapa final, com gol do seu principal jogador e artilheiro.\n\nImage: ARLINGTON, TEXAS - JUNE 30: Erling Haaland #9 of Norway celebrates with teammates after scoring the team's second goal during the FIFA World Cup 2026 Round Of 32 match between Cote d'Ivoire and Norway at Dallas Stadium on June 30, 2026 in Arlington, Texas. (Photo by Lars Baron/Getty Images)\n\nO primeiro tempo em Dallas mostrou duas escolas bem antagônicas de se jogar futebol. Enquanto a Costa do Marfim tentava a todo tempo explorar as jogadas em velocidade pelos lados do campo, a Noruega preferia trocar passes mais curtos e se impor com base na técnica.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNorvège 3-2 Sénégal | Groupe I | Temps forts, résumé (https://www.fifa.com/fr/articles/resume-temps-forts-norvege-senegal-groupe-i)\nciteturn3142search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; Image: EAST RUTHERFORD, NEW JERSEY - JUNE 22: Erling Haaland #9 of Norway celebrates scoring his team's third goal during the FIFA World Cup 2026 Group I match between Norway and Senegal at New York New Jersey Stadium on June 22, 2026 in East Rutherford, New Jersey.\n\n# Erling Haaland envoie la Norvège en seizièmes de finale\n\nPublié\n    23 juin 2026\n\nPlay Video\n\nRegardez les temps forts du match Norvège - Sénégal disputé au Stade de New York New Jersey le lundi 22 juin à 20h (heure locale).Regardez les temps forts du match Norvège - Sénégal disputé au Stade de New York New Jersey le lundi 22 juin à 20h (heure locale).\n\nGrâce notamment à un doublé d'Erling Haaland, la Norvège a dominé le Sénégal (3-2), lundi, et a validé son billet pour les seizièmes de finale de la Coupe du Monde.\n\n## Norvège 3-2 Sénégal | Groupe I\n\nButeurs : Marcus Holmgren Pedersen (43'), Erling Haaland (48', 58') pour la Norvège ; Ismaïla Sarr (53', 90+3') pour le Sénégal\n\nLa Norvège a assuré sa qualification pour les seizièmes de finale et a placé le Sénégal dans une situation délicate, lundi, au Stade de New York New Jersey. Les hommes de Ståle Solbakken, vainqueurs de l'Irak (4-1) lors de leur entrée en lice dans la Coupe du Monde de la FIFA 2026™, ont allumé la première mèche dès la 3e minute de jeu. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSpain crowned champions as curtain falls on FIFA World Cup 2026 in New York New Jersey (https://ar.fifa.com/organisation/news/new-york-jersey-stadium-spain-world-champions-mbappe-haaland)\nciteturn3142search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: last month; Image: Brazil v Morocco: Group C - FIFA World Cup 2026 ... Then it was Haaland’s turn as he scored twice following an opening goal by Marcus Pedersen to help Norway edge the West Africans 3-2 in the next match. ... In the last 16, Norway enjoyed arguably their finest football moment by beating Brazil 2-1, with both their goals coming, almost inevitably, from Haaland, who took his tally for the tournament to seven.\nMbappé eventually won the adidas Golden Boot with 10 goals and finished the tournament as the all-time leading scorer in the FIFA World Cup with 22.\n\nImage: France v Sweden: Round Of 32 - FIFA World Cup 2026\n\nIn the last 16, Norway enjoyed arguably their finest football moment by beating Brazil 2-1, with both their goals coming, almost inevitably, from Haaland, who took his tally for the tournament to seven. History was also made for Brazil as Neymar converted a late penalty to become only the second player from his country, after Pelé, to score in four FIFA World Cup tournaments. Shortly afterwards he announced his international retirement – ending his Brazil career in the same stadium where it had begun, 16 years previously, in a friendly against the United States.\n\nImage: A general view of fireworks during the trophy ceremony after Spain won the 2026 World Cup football tournament final match between Spain and Argentina at the New York/New Jersey Stadium in East Rutherford on July 19, 2026. \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHaaland, Berg and Solbakken on Norway's historical triumph (https://www.fifa.com/en/tournaments/mens/worldcup/canadamexicousa2026/articles/norway-reaction-erling-haaland-patrick-berg-stale-solbakken?searchOverlay=1)\nciteturn3142search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: last month; Match-winner Erling Haaland, midfielder Patrick Berg and coach Stale Solbakken spoke with FIFA about Norway breaking new ground at World Cup 2026. ... Image: ARLINGTON, TEXAS - JUNE 30: Erling Haaland #9 of Norway celebrates with Patrick Berg #6 after scoring the team's second goal during the FIFA World Cup 2026 Round Of 32 match between Cote d'Ivoire and Norway at Dallas Stadium on June 30, 2026 in Arlington, Texas.\n\n# Haaland: It feels unbelievable\n\nPublished\n    30 Jun 2026\n\nMatch-winner Erling Haaland, midfielder Patrick Berg and coach Stale Solbakken spoke with FIFA about Norway breaking new ground at World Cup 2026.\n\nImage: Erling Haaland #9 of Norway celebrates after the 2-1 win during the FIFA World Cup 2026 Round Of 32.\n\nEven for this pack of Vikings, these are uncharted waters.\n\nFor the first time, Norway have a knockout victory in the FIFA World Cup™ as the Scandinavian side slipped past Côte d'Ivoire in a thrilling Round of 32 tie at Dallas Stadium. As he did throughout UEFA qualifying and has done so at these global finals in North America, Erling Haaland led the way for the Norwegians, sealing a 2-1 win in the 86th minute.\n\nAudio\n\nCôte d'Ivoire v Norway | Round of 32 | FIFA World Cup 2026™ | Highlights Côte d'Ivoire v Norway | Round of 32 | FIFA World Cup 2026™ | Highlights\n\nWatch highlights of the match between Côte d'Ivoire and Norway played at Dallas Stadium on Tuesday 30 June at 12:00 (local time).--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nكوت ديفوار 1-2 النرويج | تقرير المباراة وأبرز اللقطات (https://www.fifa.com/ar/tournaments/mens/worldcup/canadamexicousa2026/articles/cote-divoire-norway-review-highlights-ar)\nciteturn3142search10 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; Image: ARLINGTON, TEXAS - JUNE 30: Odilon Kossounou #7 of Cote d'Ivoire controls the ball under pressure from Erling Haaland #9 of Norway during the FIFA World Cup 2026 Round Of 32 match between Cote d'Ivoire and Norway at Dallas Stadium on June 30, 2026 in Arlington, Texas.\n\n# هالاند يقود النرويج إلى ثمن النهائي على حساب كوت ديفوار\n\nتم النشر\n    30 يونيو 2026\n\nقاد إرلينغ هالاند منتخب النرويج إلى بلوغ دور الـ16 من كأس العالم FIFA 2026™ للمرة الأولى منذ نسخة فرنسا 1998، بعدما سجل هدف الفوز الذي منح بلاده انتصارًا ثمينًا في مواجهة كوت ديفوار.\n\nImage: FIFA\n\n## كوت ديفوار 1-2 النرويج\n\nهدف كوت ديفوار: أماد ديالو (74) أهداف النرويج: أنطونيو نوسا (39)، إرلينغ هالاند (86)\n\nقاد إرلينغ هالاند منتخب النرويج إلى التأهل لدور الـ16 من كأس العالم FIFA 2026™ للمرة الأولى منذ عام 1998، بعدما سجل هدف الفوز في الدقائق الأخيرة أمام كوت ديفوار.\n\nوشهدت المباراة بداية قوية من منتخب كوت ديفوار، الذي خاض أول مباراة إقصائية في تاريخه بكأس العالم، حيث فرض ضغطًا هجوميًا في الدقائق الأولى واعتمد على سرعة جناحيه لاختراق الدفاع النرويجي.\n\nImage: ARLINGTON, TEXAS - JUNE 30: Odilon Kossounou #7 of Cote d'Ivoire controls the ball under pressure from Erling Haaland #9 of Norway during the FIFA World Cup 2026 Round Of 32 match between Cote d'Ivoire and Norway at Dallas Stadium on June 30, 2026 in Arlington, Texas. (Photo by Julian Finney - FIFA/FIFA via Getty Images)\n\nوفي الشوط الثاني، نجح منتخب كوت ديفوار في العودة إلى أجواء اللقاء بفضل البديل أماد ديالو، الذي أدرك التعادل في الدقيقة 74 بعد مجهود فردي مميز وتسديدة قوية هزت شباك الحارس أوريان نيلاند.\n\nوبينما كانت المباراة تتجه نحو الأشواط الإضافية، ظهر النجم إرلينغ هالاند في اللحظة الحاسمة، وسجل هدف الفوز في الدقيقة 86، ليمنح النرويج بطاقة التأهل إلى دور الـ16 للمرة الأولى منذ نسخة فرنسا 1998.\n\nوسيواجه المنتخب النرويجي نظيره البرازيلي في دور الـ16، في مواجهة مرتقبة تُقام يوم 5 يوليو/تموز بمدينة نيويورك/نيو جيرسي، بينما يودع منتخب كوت ديفوار البطولة بعد مشاركة شهدت بلوغه الأدوار الإقصائية للمرة الأولى في تاريخه.\n\n* * *\n\n### إحصائية مميزة\n\nرفع إرلينغ هالاند رصيده إلى 60 هدفًا في 53 مباراة دولية بقميص منتخب النرويج، كما واصل تألقه في كأس العالم 2026 بعدما هز الشباك في مبارياته الثلاث الأولى على الإطلاق في البطولة العالمية.\n\n* * *\n\n### جائزة Michelob Ultra لأفضل لاعب في المباراة\n\nأنطونيو نوسا (النرويج)\n\n【3†Image: ARLINGTON, TEXAS - JUNE 30: Antonio Nusa #20 of Norway poses with the Michelob Ultra Superior Player of the Match Trophy during the FIFA World Cup 2026 Round Of 32 match between Cote d'Ivoire and Norway at Dallas Stadium on June 30, 2026 in Arlington, Texas. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAttempts At Goal Stats by Player | FIFA WORLD CUP 2026™ (https://www.fifa.com/en/tournaments/mens/worldcup/canadamexicousa2026/statistics/player-statistics?group=gcp